{
  "title": "Akaunting \u2014 fintech (9,817\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Akaunting\nDomain: fintech | Scale: medium | Stars: 9,817\nProblem: Online accounting software designed for small businesses and freelancers to manage invoices, expenses, budgets, and financial records. Provides a self-hosted, modular alternative to traditional accounting tools with an extensible app store ecosystem.\nTarget users: Small business owners, Freelancers, Self-employed professionals, Accountants and bookkeepers\nCore features: Invoice management and billing; Expense tracking and categorization; Financial reporting and balance sheets; Budget planning and monitoring; Modular app store for extensibility; Multi-currency and multi-language support; Calendar and payment scheduling\nIntegrations: Sentry (error tracking), FullCalendar, Stripe or payment gateways via app store, REST API for third-party integrations\nTech stack: Vue.js 2.x, Tailwind CSS, Element UI, Blade templates + Laravel 8+ (PHP 8.1+) + MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, SQLite + Apache, Nginx, IIS with Node.js for build tooling\nKey libraries: Laravel, vue-router, axios, tailwindcss, fullcalendar, flatpickr, moment.js, mathjs, vee-validate, dropzone\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Modular architecture with custom Module package enables extensible app ecosystem without sacrificing core stability\n- Blade templating combined with Vue.js for progressive enhancement allows server-rendered views with client-side interactivity\n- Self-hosted first design (on-premise focus) differentiates from SaaS competitors and appeals to privacy-conscious SMBs\n- Crowdsourced translation via Crowdin demonstrates community-driven internationalization strategy for global reach",
